## Install

::::tabs
:::tab Claude Code
```text
/plugin marketplace add bislink360/semantic-markdown
/plugin install semantic-markdown@semantic-markdown
```

The two agent skills (reading and writing `.smd`) and the MCP server, in one plugin. Or set up one project with `npx semantic-markdown init --agent claude`.
:::
:::tab Cursor, Copilot, other agents
```bash
npx semantic-markdown init --agent cursor    # or copilot, agents
```

Writes the rules file, the CLI at `.smd/smd.cjs`, the MCP server config and the `AGENTS.md` snippet into the project.
:::
:::tab VS Code
Search for **Semantic Markdown** in the Extensions view, or:

```bash
code --install-extension bislink360.semantic-markdown
```

Cursor, VSCodium and Windsurf: install the `.vsix` from the [latest release](https://github.com/bislink360/semantic-markdown/releases/latest) until the Open VSX listing is live.
:::
:::tab npm and CLI
```bash
npm install -g semantic-markdown    # the smd command
smd validate docs/
```

The same package is a zero-dependency library (`renderSmd`, `validateSmd`, `agentView`) with markdown-it, remark and rehype plugins.
:::
::::

Until the registry listings are live, every [GitHub release](https://github.com/bislink360/semantic-markdown/releases/latest) has the `.vsix`, the npm package and the skills: see the [install guide](guides/install.md). <!-- smd-disable-line link/missing-file -->

## What it looks like

````markdown
---
smd: 2
title: Saved searches
status: review
---

:::warning Breaking change
`GET /v1/search` requires the `filters` object from 2026-11-01.
:::

- [ ] Idempotent order creation :priority[P0] @api-team :due[2026-10-03]

:::decision{status=accepted owner=@maya} Accordion layout on mobile
Won usability testing on completion rate.
:::

:::agent
- All prices are integer cents.
:::
````

## For AI agents

- **One read, fewer tokens.** `smd read spec.smd` returns the whole agent view when it is small, else an outline to pick sections from. Measured: the full agent view is 5–37% smaller than the file on our sample documents, `--brief` 14–43%, and the outline plus one section about 80% smaller on 6k–8k-token documents. Small documents are cheaper to read directly.
- **Meaning is explicit.** An agent can tell an accepted decision from a proposal, a hard constraint from a side note, and its own instructions (`:::agent`) from content for people.
- **A work queue.** `smd tasks docs/` lists open tasks across documents, overdue first; the MCP server can check them off when you allow it.
- **A gate.** `smd validate` catches broken syntax, links and diagrams in CI, with fixes an agent can apply.

## For docs-as-code teams

- Every `.md` file is already valid Semantic Markdown: rename it and add structure where it helps.
- `smd export --to md` writes plain GitHub Markdown, `smd build` a static site, and the GitHub Action annotates problems on pull requests.
- Spec v2 is stable: documents written today keep their meaning in every 2.x release.

